Fixed. The bug was on line 7 of `src/import_merge.ts`: the duplicate check used a raw string comparison (`b.url === inc.url`), which is case-sensitive for the hostname, so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` were treated as different URLs and the incoming one got appended as a second entry.

The fix compares normalized URLs via the existing `normalizeUrl` helper (which lowercases the hostname), so hostname-case-only differences are now recognized as duplicates and merged (keeping the existing entry, unioning tags).

Verified: `deno check` and `deno test` both pass (3 tests green). The standalone linter's `.ts`-extension error is a false positive — the project's `deno.json` and sibling files (`bookmarks.ts`) use `.ts` import extensions consistently.


